From 2619231e9f817464cd5c70a20c1ba0c9a697f3c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:59:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/26] perf(agc): plain GPU stores for GDS, sampled queue
 choice, CPU write-back sync counter

APS5_GDS_PLAIN_STORES=1 (with APS5_GDS_GPU_STORES) records a DMA_DATA store into GDS through the new
VulkanDevice::WriteStoreOnGpu: a GPU store in queue order noted as a pending write, not a label, so a
dispatch revalidating a GDS binding does not sync through the store's batch under the GPU lock. It
falls back to WriteLabelOnGpu where a completion store, a pending label or a copied writer overlaps.
APS5_SAMPLE_QUEUE=<hex> picks the queue worker APS5_SAMPLE_WORKER samples. APS5_PROFILE_DRAW prints
[cpuwrite-sync]: the 64 KiB blocks whose pending CPU writes made CompletePendingCpuWrites sync.

Astro Bot world map: syncs on the GDS block ~300 -> 0 per 10 s, committer GPU-lock waits
~1500 -> 646 ms per 10 s, presents 101-103 -> 103-104 per 10 s; screenshot correct.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
